From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: report radar on the channel context of
 its radio

mt7996 reports a radar detection with ieee80211_radar_detected(hw,
NULL), and mac80211 then marks every channel context of the wiphy as
radar-detected. The radios of a multi-radio wiphy share one hw, so a
radar seen by one radio is also reported for the channels of the
others, and hostapd handles a radar event on each of them.

Pass the channel context of the radio whose detector fired.

Fixes: 69d54ce7491d ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: switch to single multi-radio wiphy")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -571,9 +571,15 @@
 						GFP_ATOMIC);
 	} else {
 		struct mt7996_phy *phy = mphy->priv;
+		struct ieee80211_chanctx_conf *ctx = NULL;
+
+		/* only the channel context of this radio saw the radar */
+		if (mphy->chanctx)
+			ctx = container_of((void *)mphy->chanctx,
+					   struct ieee80211_chanctx_conf, drv_priv);
 
 		phy->rdd_tx_paused = true;
-		ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, NULL);
+		ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, ctx);
 	}
 	dev->hw_pattern++;
 
